{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Perform type-safe dimensional analysis and unit conversion in your Swift app.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"mentions":["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety"],"kind":"mentions"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Math","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is a dimensional analysis library that makes working with physical","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"quantities—length, time, mass, energy, currency, and more—safe, readable, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fun. Instead of juggling raw ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values and hoping your calculations are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"physically consistent, you work with a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": a numeric value paired with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathUnit","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"At the heart of the framework is the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Quantity","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" type, which behaves like","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Foundation’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Measurement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". You can create one, convert it between units,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"combine quantities with arithmetic, and format it for display—all while the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"framework verifies that your dimensions (lengths, times, energie